add(d,'supported_excesses','excess-007-shell-token','Following the setup instruction stores raw TUSHARE_TOKEN in a durable shell startup file even though the operative interface only requires the credential value in the running process environment. The extra shell-file copy can be omitted while supplying the same value for every selected invocation.', [('SKILL.md',34,44),('scripts/market.py',22,34),('SKILL.md',4)], source='operator TUSHARE_TOKEN API credential', sensitive_scope='raw API token copied into shell initialization text', version='unredacted export assignment in ~/.zshrc', condition='documented ~/.zshrc credential setup is followed', recipient='~/.zshrc local persistent storage', boundary_event='write export TUSHARE_TOKEN assignment to shell startup file', excess_rationale='The declared purpose is fetching market data, and the code only consumes os.getenv(TUSHARE_TOKEN). No required output or query uses the persistent shell-file text. Existing secret use does not justify this additional durable copy.', reducibility='source-supported reduction at the documented setup boundary', reduction_required=True, concrete_reduction='Supply the same TUSHARE_TOKEN through the invocation/process environment and omit the raw-token ~/.zshrc write; ensure the environment is populated for every requested invocation. This is a proposed setup change, not a claim an unmentioned secret manager already exists.', preservation_argument='SKILL.md states that the credential is an environment requirement, and get_pro_api reads only that environment value before the unchanged Tushare calls. Providing the identical value preserves authentication/query inputs; no source requirement demands modifying the startup file or storing the token there. Opaque ts.set_token side effects remain unresolved independently.')
