add(d,'receiving_points','rp-008-adsets','Ad-set list/get request the explicit targeting/budget/optimization/bid/billing fields. Create sends the selected campaign/budget/optimization/bid/demographic-geographic targeting/status members; update/pause/delete have narrower shown payloads. Do not treat omitted targeting or creative values as forwarded.', [('skill.md',131,202),('skill.md',402,437)], boundary_type='network_send / model_observe of response', recipient='Meta Graph API')
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-008-ads','Ad list/get request the shown ID/status/creative/tracking/time fields. Create uses selected adset and existing creative ID, or the separate inline creative page/link/copy/CTA structure; update/pause/delete send their actual shown members. Created ad copy is intended for the selected campaign/ad delivery audience when active, not all setup secrets.', [('skill.md',206,292),('skill.md',448,455)], boundary_type='network_send / model_observe of response; intended ad publication', recipient='Meta Graph API and selected ad audience for active creative content')
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-008-creatives','Creative list returns requested object_story_spec/thumbnail fields; create sends page ID, selected link/headline/message/description/CTA. The source does not show uploading arbitrary local files or every brand-context field to this endpoint.', [('skill.md',296,325)], boundary_type='network_send / model_observe of response', recipient='Meta Graph API')
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-008-insights','Insights GETs send account/campaign/adset/ad IDs with explicit metrics and query controls; returned spend/conversion and optional age/gender breakdown data can enter model observation. Aggregates and breakdown categories are not person-level contact records.', [('skill.md',330,386),('skill.md',457,497)], boundary_type='network_send / model_observe of response', recipient='Meta Graph API; processing model for selected insight output')
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-008-pagination','The next-page example sends the account ID, id/name fields, AFTER_CURSOR and Bearer token. The documented response has cursors and a next URL, but does not establish that URLs echo tokens or that arbitrary next hosts are followed.', [('skill.md',513,539)], boundary_type='network_send / model_observe of paged response', recipient='Meta Graph API')
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-008-exchange-request','Optional extension sends APP_ID, APP_SECRET and SHORT_LIVED_TOKEN in the displayed OAuth exchange URL to graph.facebook.com. This is credential delivery to the authentication service; the source does not establish additional URL logs, browser history or other recipients.', [('skill.md',558,566)], boundary_type='network_send', recipient='Meta OAuth exchange endpoint')
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-008-exchange-return','The displayed token-exchange curl returns a JSON access_token, token_type and expires_in. When run as an agent tool with no stated isolation, the returned long-lived token plaintext can possibly enter model observation under EM02/EM03; this is separate from the necessary OAuth request.', [('skill.md',564,575),('skill.md',18),('skill.md',38,50)], boundary_type='model_observe possibility', recipient='agent-processing model', runtime_rules=['EM02','EM03','EM04'])
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-008-debug-token','Optional debug_token sends TOKEN_TO_CHECK and APP_ID|APP_SECRET to the displayed Meta endpoint. Response fields, any secret echoes and exact routing are not supplied; preserve response acquisition/model-observation possibility without inventing content.', [('skill.md',577,583)], boundary_type='network_send / model_observe of unknown response', recipient='Meta token-debug endpoint; processing model')
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-008-production-token','The separate production setup creates a System User and assigns the selected ad account and token permissions in Business Manager. Token persistence/model routing is not described; no automatic credential-file write follows merely from token creation.', [('skill.md',585,594)], boundary_type='external account configuration; returned credential handling unknown', recipient='Meta Business Manager and operator-selected runtime')
add(d,'necessary_sensitive_uses','need-008-credentials','Access tokens/app secrets are needed at the displayed authentication/API endpoints for their selected operations. The same need does not require their plaintext in the language model input or in ordinary reporting.', [('skill.md',38,50),('skill.md',564,575),('skill.md',579,583)])
add(d,'necessary_sensitive_uses','need-008-ad-data','Campaign business identifiers, budgets, targeting, creative copy and financial-performance aggregates can be sensitive, yet they are explicit inputs/outputs of selected ad-management/insight functions. No independent task narrows fields beyond the shown operation; age/gender targeting is not a supplied customer-contact list.', [('skill.md',147,169),('skill.md',330,386),('skill.md',402,437),('skill.md',457,497)])
add(d,'supported_excesses','excess-008-model-token','On the optional long-lived-token exchange branch, returning the full access_token JSON to agent processing leaves token plaintext possibly visible to the model even though the declared Ads workflow needs the token only for subsequent authentication. A local result-limited exchange can preserve the token value for requests while returning status/expiry instead.', [('skill.md',10,12),('skill.md',18),('skill.md',38,50),('skill.md',558,575)], source='Meta OAuth token-exchange response', sensitive_scope='long-lived access_token credential plaintext', version='raw token JSON returned by the displayed curl command', condition='user-token extension branch is selected and tool response is processed by the agent without isolation', recipient='agent-processing language model', boundary_event='possible model observation of raw OAuth exchange stdout under EM02/EM03', excess_rationale='The extension endpoint supplies a credential for authenticated Ads calls; no declared management/insights result requires the model to read its secret bytes. Status/expiry and the unchanged credential delivered locally to the request mechanism preserve that function.', reducibility='concrete local result-routing proposal supported by displayed response fields and environment/header interface', reduction_required=True, concrete_reduction='Capture the token exchange response in a local process, parse access_token into a model-invisible variable/credential handle for the same subsequent API requests, and return only success/token_type/expires_in or a redacted error. This is a proposed mechanism, not a claimed current protection.', preservation_argument='The source explicitly defines META_ACCESS_TOKEN for request authentication and shows access_token/token_type/expires_in in the exchange response. Keeping the exact access_token locally available preserves authenticated operations; returning nonsecret status/expiry preserves confirmation without token plaintext. Do not replace the OAuth exchange parameters without its unprovided service contract, and do not claim existing credential isolation.')
add(d,'unknowns','unknown-008-service','Meta response contents outside shown examples, provider retention/logging, token-debug output and exact authorization/permission enforcement are opaque. Query-string credentials alone do not prove extra recipients, while null retention does not prove absence of logs.', [('skill.md',38,50),('skill.md',513,527),('skill.md',577,594)])
add(d,'unknowns','unknown-008-user-task','No independent user task identifies a particular account, selected metrics/fields, acceptable target audience or confidentiality restriction. Broad read/write functionality does not prove each field necessary for every later task, but does not establish a removable excess in every example.', [('skill.md',10,12),('skill.md',58,83),('skill.md',330,386)])
