add(d,'receiving_points','rp-010-themes','Optional custom-theme installation consumes a local CSS file or network CSS URL and may persist installed theme content through wenyan. Temporary custom-theme use, list/removal and render are distinct modes; no article or secret upload to a theme author is shown.', [('SKILL.md',144,169),('references/themes.md',43,81)], boundary_type='conditional external_tool / storage_write / network fetch', recipient='wenyan theme store and selected remote CSS host')
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-010-install','If wenyan is missing, the wrapper runs npm install -g @wenyan-md/cli before loading fallback credentials. Installation writes package files and can contact the package service; installed dependency behavior and ambient environment handling are not supplied.', [('scripts/publish.sh',18,31),('scripts/publish.sh',138,144)], boundary_type='conditional external_tool / package storage and network', recipient='npm package service and global local package installation')
add(d,'receiving_points','rp-010-debug-help','Optional DEBUG=wenyan:* publishing enables detailed external CLI logs and the guide suggests inspecting errors/issues or submitting a new issue. Actual log fields, persistence, redaction and submitted issue contents are unspecified; no automatic issue upload is implemented in the retained scripts.', [('references/troubleshooting.md',259,273),('references/troubleshooting.md',277,295)], boundary_type='conditional model_observe / potential later user-selected issue publication', recipient='processing model; issue readers only if separately submitted')
