add(d,'supported_excesses','excess-010-tools-secret','The documented setup persists AppSecret plaintext in TOOLS.md even though the script already accepts complete environment credentials without reading that file. Omitting the document copy while supplying the identical values preserves the declared publishing result.', [('README.md',35,51),('README.md',185,191),('scripts/publish.sh',33,65)], source='operator WeChat Official Account AppSecret', sensitive_scope='WECHAT_APP_SECRET plaintext export assignment', version='raw secret copied into workspace credential documentation', condition='README TOOLS.md credential-storage setup is followed', recipient='workspace TOOLS.md local persistent storage', boundary_event='write AppSecret export line to TOOLS.md', excess_rationale='The declared result is an authenticated Markdown draft/image upload. The source supplies a direct environment mode and a source-code guard that skips TOOLS.md when both environment values are present, so this document copy is not required by that result.', reducibility='source-supported setup reduction using existing environment path', reduction_required=True, concrete_reduction='Supply both existing WECHAT_APP_ID and WECHAT_APP_SECRET values to the publishing process through the documented temporary environment mode and omit the plaintext AppSecret TOOLS.md entry. Keep credentials available to every requested publication without printing them.', preservation_argument='README.md shows direct environment-based wenyan publishing; publish.sh load_credentials only reads TOOLS.md when at least one environment value is absent. The same selected article/theme/highlight and valid credentials reach the unchanged publish command. This is a proposed storage reduction, not a claim the current script redacts TOOLS.md or that environment lifetime is independently secured.')
add(d,'supported_excesses','excess-010-shell-secret','The optional permanent-shell setup adds an AppSecret plaintext copy in ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc despite the same guide documenting a temporary export mode and the script consuming only current environment values.', [('references/troubleshooting.md',61,84),('scripts/publish.sh',33,65),('README.md',185,191)], source='operator WeChat Official Account AppSecret', sensitive_scope='WECHAT_APP_SECRET plaintext export assignment', version='raw secret copied into shell startup text', condition='permanent shell credential-setup alternative is selected', recipient='~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc local persistent storage', boundary_event='write AppSecret export line to shell initialization file', excess_rationale='Repeated publishing requires the credential value at each invocation, but no declared functional requirement needs the shell-startup file itself or this additional durable plaintext copy. The guide supplies a concrete temporary mechanism.', reducibility='source-supported conditional setup reduction', reduction_required=True, concrete_reduction='Use the documented temporary environment export/injection for each requested publish invocation and omit the AppSecret line in shell startup files. Supply both credential values so the existing wrapper does not fall back to missing TOOLS.md contents.', preservation_argument='The guide explicitly distinguishes temporary and permanent settings; both feed the same environment variables tested by publish.sh. Keeping those values available for each invocation preserves authentication and draft output. This does not assert every future unattended deployment has an established ephemeral credential provider.')
